  "prompt": "Build ASCII Type Explode as a native300×320px component. Make a small live ASCII message editor. Start with HELLO so the glyph effect is visible. Use a roomy Inter input below a clean raster field; edits assemble and deletion scatters actual glyph cells. Keep visible interface text in regular Inter400–500. Literal ASCII/bitmap glyph rendering and terminal code retain their intentional fixed-width character metrics. Preserve real interactive states, polite announcements, keyboard focus, cancellation, resize cleanup and reduced-motion alternatives. Hide technical headers and decorative readout/footer panels without removing nodes used by the behavior. Use the native text editing model: typed input, selection replacement, paste, deletion and cursor movement must edit the actual input value. Reconcile that value into glyph cells while preserving the caret; Escape clears. Do not append every beforeinput event blindly. Accessibility: expose the component-local content without document-level landmarks; use valid named control roles and the complete list, row and cell ownership for this composition. Preserve all visible copy, native geometry, supplied assets, datasets, interaction models and motion recipes.",
